{"src":"Ice sheet extent through the last deglaciation, 25,000 years ago to today, 0.5 degree grid (rows north to south from 90N, columns east from 180W). Values: 0 never iced, 1 iced today, 2-51 = last iced (v-1)/2 thousand years before 1950. Thickness over 20 m counts as ice. From ICE-NADI-1 (North America) merged with ICE-7G (rest of the world): Lucas, Kodama, Pico, Stoker, Lesnek, Dalton (2026), Zenodo doi:10.5281/zenodo.24204118, CC BY 4.0; ICE-7G: Roy & Peltier 2017, 2018.","w":720,"h":360,"rle":""}